WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.914
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.914 --> 00:00:04.490
SPEAKER: In this
video, we're going

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.250
to discuss committed use
discounts and sustained use

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.270
discounts.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.980
We'll provide a
brief explanation

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.630
of what they are,
how to use them,

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.670
and how to track them
in your billing account.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.360
Let's get started.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.350
First up, committed
use discounts or CUDs

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.140
provide discounted prices
for certain cloud services

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.230
in exchange for committing to
a consistent amount of usage

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.910
for a one or three-year period.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.880
There are two types of CUDs--

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.450
spend-based and resource-based.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.450
Spend-based CUDs provide
a discount in exchange

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.540
for your commitment to spend
a minimum amount for a service

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.590
each month.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.860
They are purchased and measured
in terms of dollars per hour.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.890
A limited number of services
support spend-based commitments

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.410
such as Cloud SQL.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.200
As you can see in this
example Cloud SQL CUD,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.340
the commitment amount is defined
based on the on-demand price.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.590
You then agree to pay a
monthly discounted fee

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.580
for the commitment for
the duration of the term.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.590
For some services,
like Cloud SQL,

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.140
the CUD is purchased
for a specific region

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.120
and is applied towards
all service usage

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.710
within that region.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.200
Other Cloud Services
apply spend-based CUDs

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.070
towards all usage
across all regions.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.420
Resource-based CUDs,
on the other hand,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.750
provide a discount in
exchange for your commitment

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.810
to run a certain amount
of resources continuously

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.190
each month.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.530
For example, Compute
Engine CUDs are

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.010
measured in terms of the amount
of resources such as vCPUs

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.650
and memory and work on most
Compute Engine machine types,

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.370
including predefined and
custom machine types.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:38.810
You can make
separate commitments

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.200
for GPUs and local SSD as well.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.940
Discounts apply to the aggregate
number of vCPUs, memory, GPUs,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.440
and local SSDs within a region.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.830
So they are not affected by
changes to your instances

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.760
machine setup.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.940
Like some spend-based
CUDs, resource-based CUDs

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.150
are purchased on a
per region basis.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.940
Let's head into the console
and see how to view, purchase,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.730
and track usage for your CUDs.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.370
First up, spending-based CUDs.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.039
We'll start with a
viewing your CUDs.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:13.950
For this task, you must be a
billing account administrator

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.130
or billing account viewer on
the Cloud Billing account.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.460
From the navigation
menu, select Billing.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.110
If you have more than
one Cloud Billing

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.235
account, choose the billing
account for which you'd

00:02:24.235 --> 00:02:26.520
like to view associated CUDs.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.510
Then in the left-hand navigation
menu, select Commitments.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.370
On the Commitments
Landing page, you'll

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.500
see a summary of your
committed use discounts

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.180
by commitment type.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.940
To view a detailed analysis
of a specific spend-based

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.860
commitment, you can
select it from the list.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.430
Next up, to purchase
spend-based CUDs,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.330
you must be a billing account
administrator for the account.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.210
At the top of the
screen, click Purchase.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.230
This will bring up a dialog box.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.840
Choose the product
in the dropdown

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.760
and then complete the details.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.590
Review the commitment
summary and terms

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.750
and then click Purchase.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.188
Finally, to analyze
spend-based CUDs,

00:03:03.188 --> 00:03:04.980
you must be a billing
account administrator

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.890
or a billing account viewer
on the Cloud Billing account.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.530
In the left-hand
navigation menu,

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.020
select Commitment Analysis.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.690
This page shows the details
of the selected commitment

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.880
for the period
specified in the filter,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.950
including summary
cards, a stacked bar

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.030
chart, and a summary table
of the commitment's totals.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.250
More details on reading
the Analysis page

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.530
can be found in the
documentation linked below.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.280
Next up, viewing,
purchasing, and analyzing

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.340
resource-based commitments
for Compute Engine.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.380
To view commitments
for Compute Engine,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.810
you must be a compute
admin or compute viewer

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.900
on the project in which you
purchase the commitments.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.930
Make sure you have selected
the correct project, then

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.760
head to the left-hand
navigation menu

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.380
and choose Compute Engine,
then Committed Use Discounts.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.380
This will bring you to a list of
your commitments, their status,

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.450
and additional details.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.790
To purchase commitments
for Compute Engine,

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:04.050
you must be a compute admin on
the project or a project owner.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.090
To purchase a
machine-type commitment,

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.690
click the Purchase Commitment
button at the top of the page,

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.210
name your commitment,
and complete the details,

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.790
then click Purchase.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.040
To analyze your Compute
Engine commitments,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.980
you can use the same process
as spend-based commitments.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.440
This means you must be a
billing account administrator

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.540
or billing account viewer
on the Cloud Billing

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.820
account associated with
the project containing

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.800
the commitments.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.110
From the navigation
menu, select Billing.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.960
Choose the billing account
associated with the project.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.410
In the left-hand navigation
menu, select Commitments,

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.800
then click on Compute
Engine Commitment Analysis.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.350
This page shows the details
of the selected commitment

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.360
for the period
specified in the filter,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.460
including summary
cards, a stacked bar

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:52.190
chart, and a summary table
of the commitment's totals.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:53.590
This is also where
you can change

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.840
the scope of your
Compute Engine CUDs

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.940
from project level,
which is default,

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.560
to billing account level.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.780
With discount sharing
enabled, the CUDs

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.380
apply across all eligible usage
and all projects associated

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.050
with this billing account.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.910
Any Compute Engine
resources that

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.220
do not qualify for
committed use discounts

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:16.640
automatically qualify for
sustained use discounts.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.310
Sustained use discounts
are automatic discounts

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.020
for running specific
Compute Engine

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.850
resources a significant
portion of the billing month.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.490
Sustained use discounts
give you up to 30%

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.890
off, whereas committed
use discounts give you

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:33.460
up to 57% to 70% off.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.970
SUDs require no commitment
and are applied automatically

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.970
when you meet the requirements
through your resource usage

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.610
without any action on your part.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.980
SUDs will automatically
appear on your bill

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.200
at the end of the billing cycle.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.540
You can view your
sustained use discounts

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.410
on the cost breakdown page
located in the left-hand nav.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.350
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

